Cell[TextData[StyleBox[" THIS VERSION OF THE 2026-01-30 HANDOUT WAS \
WORDSMITHED AFTER CLASS.\n\nCapacitance is an extremely important subject, \
and probably it deserves a handout just titled \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Capacitance,\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] but in this \
handout I am going to start with voltage dividers and soon you\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll see why they are closely related. A \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]voltage divider\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] is another way \
to think about resistors in series.",
 FontSize->18,
 FontSlant->"Italic"]], "Subtitle",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.97728965813264*^9, 3.97728966770008*^9}, {
