Cell[TextData[{
 "BTW, I paid $12 for that image and I am required to give credit, and it is \
good to do that anyway, even if it isn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t required. It is by \
ser_igor, and is available on istockphoto.com \
https://www.istockphoto.com/vector/li-ion-battery-diagram-gm825367806-\
133778177.\n\nI have zero clue (well, not quite zero) what is being shown. \
What I do know is that when you package this kind of chemistry into a battery \
you can by, electrons ",
 StyleBox["really want",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to come out of the end of the battery that is flat and go into the end \
with the button. By ",
 StyleBox["\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]really want\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " I mean that when one electron with charge ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", "1.6"}], 
    SuperscriptBox["x10", 
     RowBox[{"-", "19"}]], 
    StyleBox["C",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f98fcba2-1a36-4d5e-90c5-430b6fcbc18d"],
 " leaves the flat (minus) end, it \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]falls upward\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] through 1.6V of potential through the circuit to the \
button (plus) end, and in doing so, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"1.6", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["10", 
      RowBox[{"-", "19"}]], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["C",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox[" ",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Cross]", " ", "1.6"}], 
     StyleBox["V",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
    StyleBox["=",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["2.56",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox[" ",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["10",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      RowBox[{"-", "19"}]], 
     StyleBox["J",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4d190f51-b00b-40c5-8178-41ac6bbc1f5d"],
 " of energy is available to be used by the circuit.\n\nWhat if 3mA of \
current runs out of the battery for 10 minutes? How many Joules is that? \
Remember our 102g tangerine? How high could a motor using that amount of \
energy lift that tangerine? Assume (for simplicity) perfect efficiency, which \
is bogus, but still, it is a good calculation, and feel free to put in a \
factor of 0.3 for 30% efficiency if you want to make it more realistic.\n\n\
The only difference between a capacitor and a battery is that a capacitor can \
be charged and discharged essentially an infinite number of times. Some \
capacitors have finite lifetimes due to the chemicals in them eventually \
decaying, but the lifetimes are measured in many years, and you might charge \
and discharge them thousands of times per second for all those years, which \
would be something like ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["10", "11"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c03720ab-5549-4cd8-a71e-0e3421ac11a2"],
 " charges and discharges.\n\n",
 StyleBox["So why don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t we use capacitors instead of \
batteries?!?",
  FontSlant->"Italic"]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978766364393445*^9, 3.97876646668801*^9}, {
  3.978766641401043*^9, 3.978766854009482*^9}, {3.9787674531483507`*^9, 
  3.978767478526486*^9}, {3.978767527697895*^9, 3.9787676492103443`*^9}, {
  3.978768097373432*^9, 3.978768662542532*^9}, {3.978768744597712*^9, 
  3.9787688796979303`*^9}, {3.979369107588459*^9, 3.979369114707117*^9}, {
  3.979369190323213*^9, 3.979369239585791*^9}, {3.9793716188355207`*^9, 
  3.979371786572433*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"27894c34-37fa-4473-8636-\
24310e693fde"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Capacitance", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9772897343047647`*^9, 3.977289742778789*^9}, {
  3.977557185041368*^9, 3.977557199818494*^9}, {3.977560920391399*^9, 
  3.9775609285410013`*^9}, {3.977561704893649*^9, 3.9775617124536877`*^9}, {
  3.977562699357638*^9, 3.977562712075577*^9}, {3.977935734236527*^9, 
  3.977935734945239*^9}, {3.977939102048142*^9, 3.977939102844123*^9}, {
  3.977989437232789*^9, 3.977989437465143*^9}, {3.977989470213393*^9, 
  3.977989508390332*^9}, {3.97798954149605*^9, 3.977989543660515*^9}, {
  3.977990021719898*^9, 3.977990078606063*^9}, {3.977992894877846*^9, 
  3.97799289522244*^9}, {3.978139264324004*^9, 3.978139271216731*^9}, {
  3.978139302793354*^9, 3.978139304471149*^9}, {3.978766340445903*^9, 
  3.978766347061178*^9}, {3.9787667500384197`*^9, 3.9787667571611843`*^9}, {
  3.978768675909679*^9, 3.978768696639887*^9}, {3.9787688855000563`*^9, 
  3.978768888733259*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0160c44c-203d-422a-b807-\
0030eacb0aaf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A capacitor is a circuit element that obeys this law (which like Ohm\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s Law is not a law):\n\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"v", "=", 
    FractionBox["q", "C"]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FontSize->18,ExpressionUUID->"06c38466-520e-4742-8b97-df7b192e7000"],
 StyleBox["\n",
  FontSize->18],
 "\nNotice that we have an italic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["V", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ec713340-694b-41ac-a1cd-1a502e3b3ad9"],
 " and an italic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["C", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f11448eb-15e9-4f3a-803e-3256923aa2c8"],
 " in that equation. And I am not going to go insert Gothic script characters \
anymore to help you distinguish, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["V", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "49c05eb5-c69c-4dcf-a498-c41279a904e4"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["C", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "95b5259a-046e-417a-b5f4-87934e22a996"],
 " from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["V",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a8ef8f92-4ca2-4a47-887f-7af602c11ce8"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["C",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "89684bab-aac5-4b77-940e-3ba1326e4e76"],
 ". Sorry, there is only so much typesetting and word-smithing I can \
realistically do, and the italics key-combination is so much handier than \
bringing up a Gothic script palette.\n\nThe ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["V", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "9aff32ff-4589-40b5-ac5a-87497c4e9ae5"],
 " in the formula is the voltage of the capacitor. The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["q", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ecff143b-9891-425a-954f-b24ef2f8ce5e"],
 " is how much charge the capacitor is holding. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["C", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "9efeb875-8e5a-4413-8804-e27d31099690"],
 " is a property of the capacitor design called the capacitance. \n\nWhen we \
say the capacitor is \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]charged\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
or there capacitor is \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]holding charge,\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] there is a loophole in the language. The capacitor \
is always holding net zero charge inside of it. What \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]charged\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] means is that the \
capcitor has ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["q", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e6751de8-a908-4151-90f5-abb2471e61d3"],
 " of charge connected to one terminal and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", "q"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "382e5891-0b46-4f1e-baf7-e1496645ccdc"],
 " of charge connected to the other terminal, and the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["q", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f6f8ac9b-0475-4fa5-b887-1e22c6717bf5"],
 " of charge ",
 StyleBox["really wants",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to go through the circuit and combine with the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", "q"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f69f8a8a-5b53-4813-88f7-99358d57d7ee"],
 " and when it is allowed to, the capacitor will be \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]discharged, \[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] just like a \
battery.\[LineSeparator]\[LineSeparator]Here is the simplest circuit that can \
charge a capacitor:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978768919926632*^9, 3.978769149469356*^9}, {
  3.978769240461761*^9, 3.9787692410074577`*^9}, {3.9787692884346743`*^9, 
  3.978769426305768*^9}, {3.978769496557528*^9, 3.9787695462685423`*^9}, {
  3.979369287876486*^9, 3.9793693360243063`*^9}, {3.9793693788109493`*^9, 
  3.979369396840089*^9}, {3.979373226442856*^9, 3.979373232681341*^9}, {
  3.979373407052183*^9, 
  3.979373453171644*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ea096c50-ce48-4104-b898-\
804a94efc031"],

