Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The Unit of Capacitance", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
1:eJxTTMoPSmViYGAQBmIQvejASQaRRW8dr7++wQiiHwcpzpgGpKUMf80E0eFt
PNkzgPQjf8EcEH1shsxZED2nhe8ciD5amO05E0grZDN5g+iFE4/n+S9+65hm
fw9MJ3YdFA4E0nzMt8E0U/Hy5ZlAuuTROjAtd+XYahA9q7ZnA4hecn/9FhD9
QekrmM7g3P4BRN9LufwdRAeI3wnPBtJWcs/BtF0c14VNQLrs/TMwrZF88wqI
Xi7MfxVEX3PpY3i65K2jztdERhC9x+qgMYjO0VhqAqLFZWpVngHpL5Ui6iC6
jGGDHYi+UyZuD6IFykO2gulTB8E0AM8EpeQ=
  "],ExpressionUUID->"9c14f0a6-fcac-44da-bde6-2851efb86027"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Look at the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]law\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] that applies \
to capacitors:\n\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"v", "=", 
    FractionBox["q", "C"]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FontSize->18,ExpressionUUID->"5b125fee-b288-4630-9dfb-28a0ffded2fd"],
 "\n\nNotice that the proportionality constant ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["C", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e37ae15a-25a6-40cd-a6d1-e6a22b1e2e19"],
 " is in the denominator (and is italicized to distinguish it from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["C",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c547d57-23b4-41ea-a092-5df3ee426068"],
 ", the abbreviation for the Coulomb unit). This is unlike Ohm\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s Law  (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"V", "=", 
     RowBox[{"I", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "R"}]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "34f65f68-fe85-468a-8d37-ce3d816bd7e7"],
 ", where the proportionality constant ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["R", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "341ed4ea-e945-44d4-9bb8-54677c74b813"],
 " is in the numerator when you solve for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["V", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "17f450d1-638b-4338-b34a-c4640087b0f0"],
 ". You can rearrange the capacitance formula to get the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["C", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "8dbc091d-7617-4fce-91db-7acfe727cb3c"],
 " in the numerator:\n\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"q", "=", 
    RowBox[{"C", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "V"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"a3551a37-f209-4522-a1a2-bf323a3c7fca"],
 "\n\nThe way to think about that, when comparing capacitors with different \
capacitances, is to say that for a given voltage, the bigger capacitor will \
hold more charge.\n\nAGAIN, REMEMBER, WE ARE USING A LOOPHOLE IN THE LANGUAGE \
when we say \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]charged\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] or \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]holds charge.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] A capacitor is \
always net neutral, like any circuit element. But it has charge within it \
that really wants to go from one connector through the circuit and get to the \
other connector where it can combine with the opposite charge that is waiting \
there.\n\nRearrange yet again, but this time solve for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["C", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "6b7c472b-deac-43bd-8217-265bd8cff1a7"],
 ":\n\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["C",
     FontSize->16], "=", 
    FractionBox["q", "V"]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FontSize->18,ExpressionUUID->"38d7c28b-abc7-4c2e-9b60-263eb4e8831b"],
 "\n\nThe right-hand side (RHS) has units of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["Coulomb", "Volt"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "6453b9a4-f25a-4ebe-bf0c-fda29f8c812a"],
 ". I can tell you, without you having to back through all the previous \
handouts, that we have never had that combination!\n\nAnd that combination is \
going to come up so often when dealing with capacitors that for convenience \
we could really use a name for it. It is the Farad (abbreviated F), named \
after Michael Faraday:\n\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"1", 
     StyleBox["F",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"1", 
      StyleBox["C",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     RowBox[{"1", 
      StyleBox["V",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ccdbcfd5-b105-451c-99fa-3b4485f6d09e"],
 "\n\nFaraday is the guy that discovered the properties of coils of wire that \
allowed Westinghouse to design the generators and motors that Nunn first used \
in mining in Utah."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978768919926632*^9, 3.978769149469356*^9}, {
  3.978769240461761*^9, 3.9787692410074577`*^9}, {3.9787692884346743`*^9, 
  3.978769426305768*^9}, {3.978769496557528*^9, 3.9787695462685423`*^9}, {
  3.978769850874934*^9, 3.9787702444135447`*^9}, {3.9787702881720037`*^9, 
  3.9787705093896523`*^9}, {3.978770545542075*^9, 3.978770595743319*^9}, {
  3.979369457338833*^9, 3.9793694783678226`*^9}, {3.979369527604295*^9, 
  3.979369755283086*^9}, {3.979373478418723*^9, 3.979373484567195*^9}, {
  3.9793737448139*^9, 
  3.979373751683721*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"96634f8a-27a9-4198-9969-\
d25eece479f6"],

Cell["", "PageBreak",
 PageBreakBelow->True,ExpressionUUID->"b0266669-34d6-4da4-87dc-0450b74dd35c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Charging the Capacitor", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
1:eJxTTMoPSmViYGAQBWIQvejASQaRRW8dr7++wQiiHwcpzpgGpKUMf80E0eFt
PNkzgPQjf8EcEH1shsxZED2nhe8ciD5amO05E0grZDN5g+iFE4/n+S9+65hm
fw9MJ3YdFA4E0nzMt8E0U/Hy5ZlAuuTROjAtd+XYahA9q7ZnA4hecn/9FhD9
QekrmM7g3P4BRN9LufwdRAeI3wnPBtJWcs/BtF0c14VNQLrs/TMwrZF88wqI
Xi7MfxVEX3PpY3i65K2jztdERhC9x+qgMYjO0VhqAqLFZWpVngHpL5Ui6iC6
jGGDHYi+UyZuD6IFykO2gulTB8H0wZSlEs+B9FlmFUkQPeu7jRaIviw8RRtE
AwCslbdV
  "],ExpressionUUID->"ada621c5-242e-404c-8572-dec947b1341f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "If you have had a bunch of calculus, it is pretty easy to analyze the RC \
circuit. I am not assuming calculus in this course, so we will use a \
non-calculus approach called \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]numerical analysis.\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] Even if you know calculus, numerical analysis \
provides a useful way to think about RC circuits.\n\nSuppose the RC circuit \
previously drawn has been connected to the battery for a very long time.\n\n\
What is the state of the circuit? In particular, what is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["V", "C"], "(", "t", ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b4782344-410d-4b39-881b-07a2ce0e541c"],
 "? Seminar on that! What is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["q", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d590c481-8911-4945-97d1-edf52140c27c"],
 ", the charge the capacitor is holding? What is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["I", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "faa4efcf-abe1-4ad0-824e-f1311a82af0b"],
 "? Again, you are only being asked what must happen after a very long time."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978768919926632*^9, 3.978769149469356*^9}, {
  3.978769240461761*^9, 3.9787692410074577`*^9}, {3.9787692884346743`*^9, 
  3.978769426305768*^9}, {3.978769496557528*^9, 3.9787695462685423`*^9}, {
  3.978769850874934*^9, 3.9787702444135447`*^9}, {3.9787702881720037`*^9, 
  3.9787705093896523`*^9}, {3.978770545542075*^9, 3.978770595743319*^9}, {
  3.9787706722513027`*^9, 3.9787708837567463`*^9}, {3.9793698137129107`*^9, 
  3.979369940663829*^9}, {3.979373577350606*^9, 3.979373578037386*^9}, {
  3.9793737016307373`*^9, 
  3.979373701955368*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e3936a37-1078-4836-aa23-\
e76cd989d0c0"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Discharging the Capacitor \[LongDash] Throw the Switch", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
1:eJxTTMoPSmViYGAQB2IQvejASQaRRW8dr7++wQiiHwcpzpgGpKUMf80E0eFt
PNkzgPQjf8EcEH1shsxZED2nhe8ciD5amO05E0grZDN5g+iFE4/n+S9+65hm
