Cell[TextData[{
 "This graph might look familiar. It is called \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]exponential decay\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and the \
function that goes through all the points shown is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"V", "(", "t", ")"}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["V", "0"], 
     SuperscriptBox["e", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "t"}], "/", "RC"}]]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "3db58475-548e-4082-b077-c64a527098b3"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979374034822875*^9, 
  3.979374043216832*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3127f19a-5872-43a5-9f0f-\
127b0aac13e6"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Discharging the Capacitor \[LongDash] Discussion", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
1:eJxTTMoPSmViYGCQBGIQvejASQaRRW8dr7++wQiiHwcpzpgGpKUMf80E0eFt
PNkzgPQjf8EcEH1shsxZED2nhe8ciD5amO05E0grZDN5g+iFE4/n+S9+65hm
fw9MJ3YdFA4E0nzMt8E0U/Hy5ZlAuuTROjAtd+XYahA9q7ZnA4hecn/9FhD9
QekrmM7g3P4BRN9LufwdRAeI3wnPBtJWcs/BtF0c14VNQLrs/TMwrZF88wqI
Xi7MfxVEX3PpY3i65K2jztdERhC9x+qgMYjO0VhqAqLFZWpVngHpL5Ui6iC6
jGGDHYi+UyZuD6IFykO2gulTB8H0wZSlEs+B9FlmFUkQPeu7jRaIviw8RRtE
p3jmmoDoU0mzwPScGMscEB23YzmYXrB0u/QLIB39m1sGRKetzZXiXfbWkY1x
MpgGAPhH2GM=
  "],ExpressionUUID->"dc3ac547-ae20-4467-a696-b5fb053d94eb"],

Cell["\<\
When you solve the RC discharge numerically with time steps of 0.1s, you don\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t get the exact answer, but you get something pretty close, \
and you can improve the precision by taking the time steps smaller, like \
0.01s. What I had Mathematica tabulate and plot was the exact answer.

Exponential decay shows up in radioactivity. Its close friend, exponential \
growth, shows up in population dynamics. If your principal in a bank account \
is growing thanks to compounded interest, exponential growth is also \
applicable.

To summarize, understanding the numerical analysis in the RC circuit gives \
you intuition about what a capacitor does, and how the exponential can show \
up in a physical situation. Finally all this pays off in unexpected \
understanding of equations and results in seemingly unrelated fields.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978768919926632*^9, 3.978769149469356*^9}, {
  3.978769240461761*^9, 3.9787692410074577`*^9}, {3.9787692884346743`*^9, 
  3.978769426305768*^9}, {3.978769496557528*^9, 3.9787695462685423`*^9}, {
